# Not needed in the image (or, for tests/qualification, deliberately kept
# out of the runtime image -- see the Dockerfile and docs/architecture/
# S1_7_CONTAINER_PORTABILITY_DESIGN_CHECKPOINT.md, "Runtime image-content
# boundary"). The Dockerfile COPYs specific paths (pyproject.toml, README.md,
# LICENSE, python/) rather than `COPY . .`, so most of these only matter if
# that ever changes -- kept anyway as the documented, enforced boundary.
